{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 714 days after the shortage posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D12"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the azacitidine shortage on 2020-12-18 and it remains current as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["E43", "D14"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our Corvale General and Corvale East inventory both carry NDC 16729030610 labeled by Accord Healthcare Inc.",
      "cites": ["E4", "E2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "That NDC's SPL set ID 70140e11 names Intas Pharmaceuticals Limited as the manufacturing plant.",
      "cites": ["E22"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspected Intas Pharmaceuticals Limited (FEI 3004011473) ending 2022-12-02 and classified it OAI with 11 observations on the Form 483.",
      "cites": ["E18"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The OAI classification letter is dated 2023-04-05, which is 714 days after the shortage posting on 2020-12-18.",
      "cites": ["D12"]
    },
    {
      "text": "An import alert 66-40 for Intas Pharmaceuticals Limited was published on 2023-06-01 and a warning letter issued on 2023-07-28.",
      "cites": ["E20", "E19"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule-based best option is to transfer 15 units of 100 mg from Corvale General to Corvale East, which would give Corvale East 14 days on hand while Corvale General retains two weeks.",
      "cites": ["D15"]
    }
  ]
}
